h='<h1>XL330 manufacturer mechanical source comparison</h1><p><strong>NOT READY TO BUILD FROM. Original robot identity CANNOT DETERMINE.</strong> 8 September 2026. Existing source-based geometry discrepancies require review; no shelf/model changes.</p><p>Both current ROBOTIS M288 and M077 manuals link identical PDF 1986, DWG 1985 and STEP 1987 endpoints. This establishes common published nominal external geometry, not equal electrical/gear identity or the variant fitted to Microduck. No IGES link was found in those Drawings sections.</p><p>The official STEP and drawing already existed locally with recorded provenance. Their hashes match. The source STEP is a Creo DUMMY_ASSY_IDLE export dated 2020-07-27, not the internal gear design. The local parametric model reconstructs Pollen’s mesh; it does not import that STEP.</p><img style="width:100%" src="vendor-drawing.png" alt="Official ROBOTIS X330 reference drawing"><p>Original drawing: X330, 28-May-20,mm,A4 sheet1/1,FOR REFERENCE ONLY. No general tolerances or tapping thread pitch/profile specified. <a href="../../ce-parts/xl330-m288-t/iterations/v0.0.1/docs/fetched/XL,XC-330.pdf">Unchanged source PDF</a>.</p><table><tr><th>Interface</th><th>Manufacturer drawing mm</th><th>Local model mm</th><th>Finding</th></tr>'
